### Instruction:
Create a function in Java to take a paragraph as input and return a list of all the unique words in the paragraph, excluding any common stop words such as "a", "the", and "and". The function should also ignore any punctuation marks, consider the sentence to be case insensitive, and handle edge cases such as hyphenated words and contractions. Additionally, the function should implement efficient data structures and algorithms to optimize the performance of word extraction and filtering.

### Response:
Here's a possible implementation of the function:

```java
import java.util.ArrayList;
import java.util.HashSet;
import java.util.List;
import java.util.Set;

public class UniqueWordsExtractor {
    public static List<String> getUniqueWords(String paragraph) {
        // Convert the paragraph to lowercase and remove punctuation marks
        String cleanParagraph = paragraph.toLowerCase().replaceAll("[^a-zA-Z0-9\\s-']", "");

        // Define common stop words
        Set<String> stopWords = new HashSet<>();
        stopWords.add("a");
        stopWords.add("the");
        stopWords.add("and");

        // Split the paragraph into words
        String[] words = cleanParagraph.split("\\s+");

        // Filter out stop words and add unique words to a set
        Set<String> uniqueWords = new HashSet<>();
        for (String word : words) {
            // Handle hyphenated words and contractions
            if (word.contains("-")) {
                String[] hyphenatedWords = word.split("-");
                for (String hyphenatedWord : hyphenatedWords) {
                    if (!stopWords.contains(hyphenatedWord)) {
                        uniqueWords.add(hyphenatedWord);
                    }
                }
            } else {
                if (!stopWords.contains(word)) {
                    uniqueWords.add(word);
                }
            }
        }

        // Convert the set of unique words to a list and return it
        return new ArrayList<>(uniqueWords);
    }

    public static void main(String[] args) {
        String paragraph = "This is a sample paragraph. It contains some common stop words like a, the, and and. " +
                "It also includes hyphenated-words and contractions, such as doesn't and shouldn't.";

        List<String> uniqueWords = getUniqueWords(paragraph);
        for (String word : uniqueWords) {
            System.out.println(word);
        }
    }
}
```

This implementation uses a regular expression to remove punctuation marks and converts the paragraph to lowercase to make it case-insensitive. It then splits the paragraph into individual words using whitespace as a delimiter. The function filters out common stop words and adds unique words to a set to ensure uniqueness. It handles hyphenated words and contractions by splitting them if necessary. Finally, it converts the set of unique words to a list and returns it.

